      "title": "ence bottleneck caused by KV cache, particularly\nfor long content input. A series of methods (Zhang\net al., 2023; Ge et al., 2023; Liu et al., 2023c; Oren\net al., 2024) explored the sparsity among Trans-\nformer's attention block, then evicted unnecessary\ntokens from KV Cache for efficient inference. For\ninstance, H2O (Zhang et al., 2023) retained a bal-\nance of recent and heavy hitter tokens with the\nhighest accumulated attention scores throughout\nthe sequence. Scissorhands (Liu et al., 2023c) se-\nquentially predicted the potentially pivotal tokens\nwith the attention score above average within a his-\ntory window. Some method (Ge et al., 2023) further\napplied costly eviction policy selection for better",
